       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it exceeds the maximum safe acetaminophen dose.\n\n- **Dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the standard maximum single dose of 1000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This dose carries a significant risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options that fit a 70 kg adult with normal renal and hepatic function:\n1. **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3000 mg/day).\n2. **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4000 mg/day), if your institution allows the full maximum.\n3. **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2600 mg/day).\n\nDid you mean one of these, or was 2000 mg/day intended (for example, 650 mg or 500 mg per dose)? If you really want the original dose, tell me and I'll note that you've confirmed it. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
